# Add a Domain

Copy the shape of the `product` domain. It is the reference: one business
package, one Postgres store, one OTel extension, one app package, business tests
and API tests. Build from the inside out so each step compiles against the one
before it.

## Before writing code

Agree with the user on:

1. The domain name `<x>` (singular, lowercase: `order`, `invoice`).
2. The data models for the business layer: `<X>`, `New<X>`, `Update<X>`. Use
   strong types from `business/types/*`; propose a new type only when none fits
   (see `layered-architecture-types`).
3. The routes and which auth rule guards each (`auth.RuleAny`,
   `auth.RuleAdminOnly`, `auth.RuleUserOnly`, `auth.RuleAdminOrSubject`).
4. Whether the domain depends on another domain (one-way import) or must react
   to another domain's events (delegate).

## Steps

1. **Migration.** Append a new `-- Version: X.YY` block to
   `business/sdk/migrate/sql/migrate.sql`. Never edit an applied block; darwin
   checks a checksum per version. Add dev rows to `seed.sql` if useful.
2. **Strong types.** Add any new value types under `business/types/<name>/`
   with `Parse`, `MustParse`, `String`, `Equal`, `MarshalText`.
3. **Business package** `business/domain/<x>bus/`:
   - `model.go`: `<X>`, `New<X>`, `Update<X>` (pointer fields = not provided).
   - `filter.go`: `QueryFilter` with pointer fields.
   - `order.go`: `OrderBy*` constants with opaque values and `DefaultOrderBy`.
   - `<x>bus.go`: sentinel errors, `Storer`, `ExtBusiness`, `Extension`,
     `Business`, `NewBusiness` (reverse-apply extensions), `NewWithTx`, methods.
     The business layer assigns IDs and timestamps.
   - `event.go`: only if other domains must react to this one.
   - `testutil.go`: `TestNew<X>s` and `TestSeed<X>s` for other packages' tests.
4. **Store** `business/domain/<x>bus/stores/<x>db/`: `model.go` (row struct with
   `db` tags, `toDB<X>`, `toBus<X>`, `toBus<X>s`), `filter.go` (`applyFilter`),
   `order.go` (`orderByFields`, `orderByClause`), `<x>db.go` (named SQL through
   `sqldb` helpers; translate `sqldb.ErrDBNotFound` to `<x>bus.ErrNotFound`).
5. **Extension** `business/domain/<x>bus/extensions/<x>otel/`: implement every
   `ExtBusiness` method; add a span to each (see `business-layer-extensions`).
6. **Business tests** `<x>bus_test.go` using `dbtest.New` and `unittest.Run`.
7. **App package** `app/domain/<x>app/`: `model.go` (JSON models with
   `Encode`/`Decode`, `toBus*`, `toApp*`), `filter.go`, `order.go`,
   `<x>app.go` (handlers on an unexported `app` struct), `route.go` (`Config` +
   `Routes`). If routes act on one owned entity, add `mid.Authorize<X>` in
   `app/sdk/mid/authorize.go` plus `set<X>`/`Get<X>` context helpers in
   `app/sdk/mid/mid.go`.
8. **Wiring:**
   - `app/sdk/mux/mux.go`: add `<X>Bus` to `BusConfig`.
   - `api/services/<service>/main.go`: construct extension, store, business.
   - `business/sdk/dbtest/business.go`: construct it the same way; add to `BusDomain`.
   - `api/services/<service>/build/all.go`: call `<x>app.Routes`.
   - `app/sdk/apitest/start.go`: pass the new bus into `mux.BusConfig`.
9. **API tests** `api/services/<service>/tests/<x>api/`: one file per endpoint,
   table functions named by status (`create200`, `create400`, `create401`).

## Verify

```
go build ./...
go vet ./...
make test-only
```

Then run the `layered-architecture-types` conformance checklist on the new
files.
